      "model": "deepseek-chat",
      "status": "ok",
      "summary": "PR #10 reverts the demo release to the previous image digest and bumps the app.kubernetes.io/version label on Deployment, Service, and ServiceMonitor. The change is confined to gitops/demo/values.yaml, so the Git desired state is the source of truth; the revert commit plus Argo resync is the correct rollback path, and an imperative argocd app rollback or kubectl rollout undo must not be presented as a GitOps rollback. Two pod-template env values are redacted, so reviewers cannot confirm they hold normal values rather than fault-injection settings; the candidate must not carry DEMO_STARTUP_FAIL=true or DEMO_ERROR_RATE=1. Capacity evidence is weak: 35 scheduled Pods have no CPU/memory requests and are counted as zero, so free capacity is overstated, and KubeCPUOvercommit is firing. The AI result status is invalid (ERROR), so the decision preview is ERROR and this PR cannot be treated as approved. Post-sync verification should confirm rollout status, the running image digest, and the /version output."
    },
